  // design: Sandfall follow-up (owner, 2026-11-09): the Side walls option of the Vaulted Tunnel (MapMaker's tile inspector; a tile of its own, so maps need no new field). Its masonry is capped 0.25 m under the level above (a kerb at ground level), and its floors keep the terrain round it at that kerb: the passage's floor is inset 0.3 m from the closed sides, so the ground on the cell's edge there is pulled only to the cap (settle.ts terrainUnderFloors), not down to the passage; a buried floor inside each wall (-0.3 to 0.6 m) carries the ground under the wall down to the passage's floor, so no slope of earth shows in the passage. The ground over the tunnel itself must still be within 3 m of its floor (flattened), as for the plain tile.
