  // design: Tileset 04, Tunnel Systems, step 1 (owner, 2026-11-13; docs/map-briefs/tunnels/PLAN_2026-11-13.md): the Under ground option of the Vaulted Tunnel Crossing (MapMaker's tile inspector; a tile of its own, so maps need no new field). The plain tile's masonry under a cap slab 0.25 m under the level above, so it is a closed shell. Its bore (map/groundBore.ts) takes the ground's surface out of its own cell between its floor slab and its cap: a hill higher than the cap stays on top, ground that crosses the passage is gone, and ground beside the cell meets its masonry. Its floors pull no ground down (settle.ts terrainUnderFloors), and its cover keeps at least 0.1 m of earth over its cap (a level under new flat ground that is the ground as it lies: nothing is added) (a buried tunnel in a dip is a mound, never bare masonry). An end that comes out of the hill takes a Tunnel Portal.
