  // design: Flavius Rule's octagon (docs/map-briefs/sandfall_colosseum/OCTAGON_PLAN.md): made by tools/content/kit/arenaCorner.mjs. The anchor cell is the corner of the sand (the tile covers the cells 0..8 east and north of it). Its own tile (not part of the gate option, whose cells are the plain corner's), so it claims only what the corner leaves free: the outer court's cells under it at levels 0-7 and all of level 8; it stands with its inner face on the facade's outer face (depth 56 m), so the storey tiles keep the facade, and only the attic needs the gate option (the walk and roof open into it). The rows are the Seating Tier's (0.5 m by 1 m) and the podium Arena Seating's, so they meet the straight bays flush; seats in the solids slot, lips in trim, walls and vaults in walls, walkways and slabs in floor. Arches collide plain (piers and lintel; owner 2026-11-14, 6a).
